<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasekura Tsunenaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1571–1622</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasekura Tsunenaga was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-masamune">Date Masamune</a> who led a Japanese embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from 1613 to 1620. Sailing via <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, he met King Philip III and was received by Pope Paul V in 1615. By the time he returned, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> had turned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and the mission brought no lasting results.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasekura-tsunenaga.jpg" alt="Hasekura Tsunenaga" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archita Ricci, formerly attributed to Claude Déruet Claude Deruet[1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hasekura_in_Rome.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
